(ROGDI Recall Exam Answer Key) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(1. What disease is the ROGDI case study about?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Kohlschutter-Tonz syndrome, also called amelocerebrohypohidrotic syndrome.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(2. What is the Orphanet ID for the ROGDI/KTS disease case?) Tj
T*
(Answer: ORPHA:1946.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(3. What are the two OMIM identifiers used in the ROGDI audit?) Tj
T*
(Answer: OMIM phenotype 226750 and OMIM gene 614574.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(4. What is the correct gene symbol for the case study?) Tj
T*
(Answer: ROGDI.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(5. What is the correct UniProt accession for human ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Q9GZN7.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(6. What is the recommended protein name for UniProt Q9GZN7?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Protein rogdi homolog.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(7. What are three aliases for ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: KIAA0267, FLJ22386, and RAV2.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(8. What chromosome location is listed for ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: 16p12.1.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(9. What is the protein length of ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: 287 amino acids.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(10. What is the approximate molecular weight of ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: About 32.3 kDa, or 32,254 Da.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(11. What is the approximate ROGDI amino-acid coding region length?) Tj
T*
(Answer: About 861 bp, or 864 bp if the stop codon is included by convention.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Core identity) Tj
T*
T*
T*
T*
T*
(Page 1) Tj
