(ROGDI Recall Exam Answer Key \(continued\)) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(12. Why is source verification the first step before scoring a gene therapy target?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Because a wrong disease, gene, or protein identity poisons every downstream) Tj
T*
(conclusion: cargo size, mechanism, potency assay, vector fit, and risk assessment.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Source verification) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(13. Which source is used to confirm protein identity and sequence facts?) Tj
T*
(Answer: UniProt. For ROGDI, the key accession is Q9GZN7.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Source verification) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(14. Which source is used to anchor rare disease identity?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Orphanet. For this case, the disease is ORPHA:1946.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Source verification) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(15. Which source is used for disease and gene OMIM entries?) Tj
T*
(Answer: OMIM. For ROGDI/KTS, phenotype 226750 and gene 614574 are used.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Source verification) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(16. What live UniProt facts were checked for Q9GZN7?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Primary accession, protein name, gene name, sequence length, molecular weight,) Tj
T*
(and cross-references such as PDB, AlphaFoldDB, InterPro, and Pfam.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Source verification) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(17. What is the inheritance pattern of Kohlschutter-Tonz syndrome?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Autosomal recessive.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Disease biology) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(18. Why does autosomal recessive loss of function support gene addition?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Because adding a working copy of the gene can, in principle, replace missing) Tj
T*
(or reduced function.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Disease biology) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(19. What are the three classic features of KTS described in the audit?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Amelogenesis imperfecta, infantile or early-onset epilepsy, and intellectual) Tj
T*
(disability or severe neurodevelopmental impairment.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Disease biology) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(20. Name three additional clinical features reported in KTS.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Spasticity, hypohidrosis or heat intolerance, and nephrocalcinosis in some) Tj
T*
(patients.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Disease biology) Tj
T*
T*
T*
T*
T*
(Page 2) Tj
