(ROGDI Recall Exam Answer Key \(continued\)) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(21. Why does the audit prioritize CNS rescue?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Because epilepsy and neurodevelopmental impairment likely dominate morbidity) Tj
T*
(and mortality.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Disease biology) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(22. Why might dental disease be hard to reverse in KTS?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Enamel is formed during a limited developmental window and does not remodel) Tj
T*
(like bone once formed.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Disease biology) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(23. How should ROGDI be treated functionally for gene therapy planning?) Tj
T*
(Answer: As a non-secreted intracellular scaffold or adaptor protein, not as a simple) Tj
T*
(enzyme replacement target.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Protein function) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(24. What two PDB structures are linked to human ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: 5XQH and 5XQI.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Protein function) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(25. What domain or family annotations are listed for ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: RAVE2/Rogdi, Rogdi_lz, InterPro IPR028241, and Pfam PF10259.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Protein function) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(26. What 2025 biology connection is important for ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: ROGDI is connected to Rabconnectin-3-associated V-ATPase biology.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Protein function) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(27. Why does the Rabconnectin-3/V-ATPase link matter?) Tj
T*
(Answer: It gives a plausible mechanism involving acidic organelles, lysosomes,) Tj
T*
(synaptic vesicles, neurons, and enamel/mineralization biology.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Protein function) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(28. Is ROGDI secreted?) Tj
T*
(Answer: No. ROGDI is treated as intracellular and non-secreted.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Localization) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(29. Why does non-secreted localization make gene therapy harder?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Because neighboring corrected cells are unlikely to rescue uncorrected cells) Tj
T*
(by secreting the protein. The affected cells probably need direct transduction.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Localization) Tj
T*
T*
T*
T*
T*
(Page 3) Tj
