(ROGDI Recall Exam Answer Key \(continued\)) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(30. What is cell-autonomous rescue?) Tj
T*
(Answer: A therapeutic effect that requires correction inside the affected cell itself.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Localization) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(31. What is cross-correction?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Rescue of neighboring untransduced cells by a secreted therapeutic protein.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Localization) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(32. Why is cross-correction expected to be low for ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Because ROGDI is not known to be secreted.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Localization) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(33. Name three reported or annotated ROGDI localization contexts.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Nuclear envelope, axon/dendrite/perikaryon, presynapse, synaptic vesicle) Tj
T*
(context, or acidic organelle context.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Localization) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(34. What is the highest-priority therapeutic tissue for the first ROGDI program?) Tj
T*
(Answer: CNS neurons.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Target tissues) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(35. Which tooth-development cell type matters for KTS dental disease?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Ameloblasts, the cells responsible for enamel formation.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Target tissues) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(36. Why is there a brain/teeth delivery mismatch?) Tj
T*
(Answer: A CNS-directed route is not expected to robustly correct ameloblasts, and) Tj
T*
(dental-directed delivery will not rescue CNS neurons.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Target tissues) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(37. What is AAV?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Adeno-associated virus, a small non-replicating viral vector commonly used for) Tj
T*
(in vivo gene delivery.) Tj
T*
(Topic: AAV and cargo) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(38. What practical AAV packaging limit is used in the audit?) Tj
T*
(Answer: About 4.7 kb.) Tj
T*
(Topic: AAV and cargo) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(39. Why does ROGDI pass the AAV cargo-size gate?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Its coding sequence is about 861 bp, leaving large room for promoter, polyA,) Tj
T*
(ITRs, and other regulatory elements within the AAV limit.) Tj
T*
(Topic: AAV and cargo) Tj
T*
T*
T*
T*
T*
(Page 4) Tj
ET
