(ROGDI Recall Exam Answer Key \(continued\)) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(40. What first-pass vector is recommended for the ROGDI CNS proof of concept?) Tj
T*
(Answer: AAV9.) Tj
T*
(Topic: AAV and cargo) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(41. Why is AAV9 considered relevant to ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: It has clinical precedent for nervous-system exposure, especially early-life) Tj
T*
(CNS-directed gene replacement.) Tj
T*
(Topic: AAV and cargo) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(42. Does AAV9 precedent prove ROGDI efficacy?) Tj
T*
(Answer: No. It only supports platform feasibility. ROGDI-specific success still) Tj
T*
(requires direct neuronal transduction, correct localization, and valid potency assays.) Tj
T*
(Topic: AAV and cargo) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(43. What promoter is recommended for the first ROGDI CNS proof of concept?) Tj
T*
(Answer: hSYN1, a compact human synapsin-1 promoter for neuron-biased expression.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Construct design) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(44. Why use a neuron-biased promoter like hSYN1 first?) Tj
T*
(Answer: It matches the CNS objective and may reduce unnecessary peripheral) Tj
T*
(overexpression.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Construct design) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(45. What cargo would the first-pass ROGDI construct carry?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Sequence-verified human ROGDI Q9GZN7 cDNA.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Construct design) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(46. What routes are considered for CNS-prioritized ROGDI delivery?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Early-life systemic IV or intrathecal delivery, selected after biodistribution) Tj
T*
(and toxicity comparison.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Construct design) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(47. Why is a simple enzyme activity assay not enough for ROGDI?) Tj
T*
(Answer: ROGDI is not being treated as a simple catalytic enzyme. It likely works) Tj
T*
(through localization, complex interaction, and organelle/synaptic biology.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Potency assays) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(48. What should a ROGDI potency assay package measure?) Tj
T*
(Answer: Expression, intracellular localization, Rabconnectin-3 or complex interaction,) Tj
T*
(V-ATPase/acidification readouts, and cell-based rescue.) Tj
T*
(Topic: Potency assays) Tj
T*
T*
T*
T*
T*
(Page 5) Tj
